<title>AUSTRALIA: Comalco aluminium production up in qtr.</title>
<headline>Comalco aluminium production up in qtr.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Comalco Ltd, 67 percent owned by RTZ-CRA, said its primary aluminium production rose to 122,958 tonnes in the three months to March 31 from 111,701 a year earlier.</p>
<p>Aluminium sales rose to 128,375 tonnes from 106,487.</p>
<p>Production details:</p>
<p>		 3 months to  3 months to  3 months to  12 months</p>
<p>		 March 31/97  March 31/96    Dec 31/96  to Dec 31/96</p>
<p>				 (in tonnes)</p>
<p>Primary</p>
<p>Aluminium</p>
<p> Bell Bay	 34,023	25,100	34,543	119,735</p>
<p> Boyne Is	 31,028	32,842	32,545	130,157</p>
<p>Tiwai Point</p>
<p> (New Zealand)  57,907	53,759	60,849	225,912</p>
<p>Sales	    128,375     106,487     124,730	468,857</p>
<p>Weipa</p>
<p>Beneficated</p>
<p> bauxite	2,058,245   2,309,376   2,230,686   9,524,080</p>
<p>Metal grade</p>
<p> shipments    2,235,295,  2,457,660   2,518,711   9,401,616</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
